{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.7,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["R11", "C11"],
      "pins": ["U4.27"],
      "nets": ["VCOMH", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the DISPLAY sheet (display.kicad_sch), the SSD1306 VCOMH charge-pump output (U4 pin 27) is tied to GND through resistor R11, value 10k. No capacitor C11 appears anywhere on the sheet; the only left-side passive column is C7 (2.2u, VCC bypass), R5 (390k, IREF), and R11 (10k, VCOMH).",
      "expected": "The specification's OLED bias/charge-pump network states that the VCOMH output reservoir/filter cap is C11 = 4.7 µF from VCOMH to GND: 'C11 (4.7 µF) — U4 VCOMH (charge-pump output) to GND, the output reservoir/filter cap'. A capacitor belongs in this position, not a 10 kΩ resistor.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C11 (4.7 µF) — U4 VCOMH (charge-pump output) to GND, the output reservoir/filter cap"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "display.kicad_sch (page 5): resistor symbol 'R11 10k' connected between the VCOMH (pin 27) wire and GND; no C11 present on the sheet"}
      ],
      "impact": "Replacing the VCOMH reservoir capacitor with a 10 kΩ resistor loads the SSD1306 internal charge-pump output to ground and removes the output filtering, so VCOMH cannot hold the panel drive voltage. The OLED will be very dim or fail to display.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["J1", "R10"],
      "pins": ["J1.reset", "U2.7"],
      "nets": ["RESET", "NRST"],
      "observed": "On the root sheet (PCB.kicad_sch, page 1) the MCU reset net is labelled 'NRST' (U2 pin 7 and R10 to VCC), whereas the Tag-Connect J1 reset pin carries the global label 'RESET'. There is no wire and no common label joining the two, so the programmer's reset pin is not connected to the MCU NRST net.",
      "expected": "The specification states the two are on the same net: 'R10 (10 kΩ) ties NRST to VCC... NRST is also wired to J1 pin 3 (~{RESET})'. The J1 reset pin should share the NRST net so the programmer can pull it low.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R10 (10 kΩ) ties NRST to VCC, holding the MCU's NRST pin high at idle; NRST is also wired to J1 pin 3 (~{RESET})"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "PCB.kicad_sch (page 1): MCU pin 7 / R10 carry global label 'NRST'; J1 reset pin carries global label 'RESET' with no connecting wire"}
      ],
      "impact": "The SWD/Tag-Connect programmer cannot assert a hardware reset on the MCU; only software/SWD-initiated reset would work, deviating from the intended debug interface.",
      "confidence": 0.45
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing deviates from the reference in the OLED charge-pump network: the VCOMH output reservoir capacitor C11 (4.7 µF) is replaced by a 10 kΩ resistor R11, which loads the SSD1306 charge-pump output and would prevent the display from working; a secondary suspect is the J1 reset pin net 'RESET' not joining the MCU 'NRST' net as the spec requires."
}

